{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T05:40:18.216+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_2c022427-3876-4f70-9bc8-6ac0bd8ab7b8", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): so what will happen if my credit card application got rejected?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: I am asking about re-applying for a credit card.\nAI: I do not currently have the details available regarding the process for re-applying for a credit card. 💳\nUser: i just want to know can i apply again if got rejected\nAI: I currently do not have any details available about whether you can apply again for a credit card following an earlier denial. 💳\nUser: so what will happen if my credit card application got rejected?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Steps to follow after receiving a notification of credit card application rejection from the bank.\", \"policy\": \"Rules regarding waiting periods and eligibility criteria for re-submitting a new credit card application.\", \"conceptual\": \"General information about the credit card application review process and reasons for potential application denial.\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Credit_Card\", \"Deposit_Account\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Loan And Credit Management\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\"], \"customer_component\": \"Explain the consequences or process following a credit card application rejection.\", \"direct_query\": \"Explain the consequences or process following a credit card application rejection.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Steps to follow after receiving a notification of credit card application rejection from the bank.\", \"policy\": \"Rules regarding waiting periods and eligibility criteria for re-submitting a new credit card application.\", \"conceptual\": \"General information about the credit card application review process and reasons for potential application denial.\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Request a complimentary copy of your credit report following a formal notice of application decline.\", \"policy\": \"Understand the mandatory waiting period required before submitting a subsequent application for a credit card.\", \"conceptual\": \"Accessing personal credit history records to identify factors that may have influenced the bank's decision.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_adff3913\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_adff3913\"], \"reason\": \"The provided evidence explains the notification process following a credit card application rejection, which is a meaningful part of the customer's request. However, the evidence does not address the customer's specific question about whether they can apply again after a rejection.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"fact\": \"Applicants are informed of a credit card application rejection via email or text.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank provides specific reasons for credit card application denials, such as insufficient earnings or existing overdue obligations.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_adff3913\"], \"reason\": \"The evidence confirms the notification process for a rejected application, which is a component of the request. However, no evidence addresses the customer's specific question regarding the possibility of re-applying after a rejection.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_6b6d2823\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank does not disclose specific reasons for credit card application denials due to confidentiality and banking policies.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b26b6b4a\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank does not disclose specific reasons for a declined application for an additional credit card.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_adff3913\"], \"reason\": \"The evidence confirms the notification process for a rejected application, which is a component of the request. However, no evidence addresses the customer's specific question regarding the possibility of re-applying after a rejection.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_e3c2064e\", \"fact\": \"Applicants can obtain a complimentary credit report within {{faq_e3c2064e_001}} calendar days of a credit card application rejection.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_25ce7c68\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the process for requesting a waiver of charges on my Horizon Bank credit card account?\\n\\nAnswer: To request a waiver of a late payment fee, simply send a message through the Horizon App's in-app chat service, specifying 'fee waiver' in your query. Our team will carefully review your request and provide an update via push notification within {{faq_25ce7c68_001}} working days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d8b75c7d\", \"content\": \"Question: As an existing Standard Chartered credit cardholder, can I bypass the application process for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: While having an existing credit card does not exempt you from applying for a Horizon Bank credit card, our streamlined application process is designed to be efficient and hassle-free. Please note that for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents with an annual income ranging from {{faq_d8b75c7d_001}} to {{faq_d8b75c7d_002}}, your Horizon Bank credit limit will be combined with your Standard Chartered credit limit, as per regulatory requirements.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
