{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T05:40:57.904+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_2c022427-3876-4f70-9bc8-6ac0bd8ab7b8", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): ok, so after that can i apply again?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: I am asking about re-applying for a credit card.\nAI: I do not currently have the details available regarding the process for re-applying for a credit card. 💳\nUser: i just want to know can i apply again if got rejected\nAI: I currently do not have any details available about whether you can apply again for a credit card following an earlier denial. 💳\nUser: so what will happen if my credit card application got rejected?\nAI: When a credit card application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text. 💳\nUser: ok, so after that can i apply again?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Submit a new application through the online portal after the cooling-off period has elapsed.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must wait for the specified duration following a rejection before submitting a new request.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card re-application refers to the process of submitting a new request after a previous denial.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\", \"Eligibility\"], \"customer_component\": \"Inquire about the eligibility or policy for re-applying for a credit card after a previous application has been rejected.\", \"direct_query\": \"Inquire about the eligibility or policy for re-applying for a credit card after a previous application has been rejected.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit a new application through the online portal after the cooling-off period has elapsed.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must wait for the specified duration following a rejection before submitting a new request.\", \"conceptual\": \"Credit card re-application refers to the process of submitting a new request after a previous denial.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}}