cants must meet minimum age and annual income requirements to qualify for a new credit card.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card application is the formal request process for establishing a new revolving credit account.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\", \"Eligibility\"], \"customer_component\": \"What are the eligibility requirements or policies for submitting a new credit card application?\", \"direct_query\": \"What are the eligibility requirements or policies for submitting a new credit card application?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the online application form with all required personal identification and income documentation attached.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet minimum age and annual income requirements to qualify for a new credit card.\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card application is the formal request process for establishing a new revolving credit account.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permanent residents, and {{faq_b3c9ded6_007}} for foreigners with a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c241b12d\", \"content\": \"Question: As a senior citizen, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card, and what are the key requirements I need to fulfill?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we welcome applications from retirees who meet specific criteria. To qualify for our credit card with a credit limit of {{faq_c241b12d_001}}, you must be a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, aged {{faq_c241b12d_002}} or above, have an assessed annual income of less than {{faq_c241b12d_003}}, and not hold any existing credit cards or unsecured loans with us. If you meet these conditions, you may be eligible for our credit card, subject to our standard banking requirements.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - Th