ation And Security\", \"Features And Limits\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\"], \"customer_component\": \"Provide general information about the features and capabilities of the Horizon mobile application.\", \"direct_query\": \"Provide general information about the features and capabilities of the Horizon mobile application.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Access the main dashboard to view available tools and navigate through the application menu options.\", \"policy\": \"Usage of mobile application features is subject to standard security protocols and individual account permissions.\", \"conceptual\": \"The Horizon mobile application provides a digital interface for managing personal accounts and performing banking transactions.\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Verify your identity using multi-factor authentication steps required to access sensitive account management features within the app.\", \"policy\": \"All digital banking activities are protected by advanced encryption standards and automated fraud detection monitoring systems.\", \"conceptual\": \"The application security framework includes identity verification and encryption to ensure safe access to your personal financial data.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_9da9234e\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The supplied parent only provides information regarding the download source of the Horizon App, which does not address the user's request for general information about the app's features and capabilities.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_9da9234e\"], \"reason\": \"The supplied parents provide information regarding the security features of the Horizon App, which is a meaningful part of the request for general information about the app's features. Other aspects of the app's general capabilities remain unaddressed.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_9da9234e\", \"fact\": \"The Horizon mobile application uses a security framework including encryption, identity verification, fraud detection, and multi-factor authentication.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_14914805\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to immediately restrict access to my Horizon Bank mobile application if I suspect unauthorized activity?\\n\\nAnswer: To promptly block access to your Horizon Bank App, you have two convenient options. Firstly, you can enable the Kill Switch feature directly within the Horizon App by navigating to the Profile section, then selecting Security, and finally activating the Kill Switch. Alternatively, you can reach out to our dedicated customer support team via our hotline. After choosing your preferred language, simply press '{{faq_14914805_001}}' to report a suspected scam or fraud, and our agents will be happy to assist you. Additionally, you can also contact us through the Horizon App by following these straightforward steps: \\n   - Navigate to the Profile section and select 'Contact us'\\n   - Choose 'Contact Horizon for urgent matters'\\n   - Opt for either 'Talk to us via app' or 'Leave us a message via chat'\\n   - Select 'Suspected Scam or Fraud' to initiate a call or chat with our support team\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7f54cd55\", \"content\": \"Question: What happens after I enable the Horizon Bank's security lock, and how can I verify its activation?\\n\\nAnswer: Upon successful activation of the security feature, access to your Horizon App and Horizon card(s) will be immediately blocked. Additionally, AutoPay transfers from your savings account will be halted, although payments to your Horizon credit card and Savings Pot will continue to be processed. You will be logged out of any active sessions, and a confirmation SMS will be sent to your registered mobile number. To further confirm, upon re-accessing the Horizon App, a notification will be displayed indicating that the security lock is currently in effect.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ed9b5ce2\", \"content\": \"Question: What measures does Horizon Bank take to protect me from phishing scams and unauthorized transactions?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we prioritize your security and adhere to the guidelines outlined in Section {{faq_ed9b5ce2_001}} of the E-Payments User Protection Guidelines. As part of our commitment to the Shared Responsibility Framework, we have implemented several key measures to safeguard your accounts. These include: \\n   - A mandatory {{faq_ed9b5ce2_002}}-hour waiting period after activating your Horizon Key or logging in from a new device, during which certain high-risk activities such as adding new payees, increasing transaction limits, disabling notifications, or changing your contact information are restricted.\\n   - Immediate notifications: You will receive instant updates via push notifications and email for all outgoing payments, ensuring you are always informed about your transactions.\\n   - Emergency Lockdown: The Horizon App features an Emergency Lockdown option, accessible under Profile > Security, which allows you to instantly block all access to your mobile banking, account, and cards if you suspect they have been compromised.\\n   - Advanced Security Systems: As of {{faq_ed9b5ce2_003}} June {{faq_ed9b5ce2_004}}, we have enhanced our systems to provide an additional layer of protection against potential phishing scams. Some transactions may be temporarily paused for review, and you will be notified to verify the transaction. If you do not recognize the transaction, please cancel it within the {{faq_ed9b5ce2_005}}-hour timeframe provided.\\n   - Round-the-Clock Support: Our customer service is available {{faq_ed9b5ce2_006}}/{{faq_ed9b5ce2_007}}. You can reach us through the Horizon App or by calling our dedicated hotline at +{{faq_ed9b5ce2_008}} {{faq_ed9b5ce2_009}} {{faq_ed9b5ce2_010}} for immediate assistance.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b00e6476\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I regain access if I can't remember my Horizon app passcode?\\n\\nAnswer: - Choose the \\\"Forgot Passcode\\\" option in the Horizon App and follow the provided steps.\\n- For a smoother and more secure experience, we suggest activating facial recognition or fingerprint authentication.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9da9234e\", \"content\": \"Question: What protections are built into the Horizon mobile application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon employs a layered security framework that incorporates encryption, identity verification, fraud detection, and continuous real‑time monitoring to safeguard your account, transactions, and personal data.\\n- Access to the Horizon App is secured with multi‑factor authentication, and the app may be linked to only a single device and one phone number at any given time.\\n- Requiring two distinct authentication methods by default provides a robust defense against online threats.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general)