tionalities does Horizon Bank’s savings account provide?\\n\\nAnswer: - Tailored growth options: Select a savings plan that best matches your goals and earn interest on the balance you keep. Enjoy a rate of up to {{faq_26880b57_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_26880b57_002}}, with any amount above that earning {{faq_26880b57_003}} p.a.\\n- Completely fee‑free: Horizon Bank imposes no hidden charges—no minimum‑balance penalty, no fall‑below fee, no monthly maintenance fee, no account‑closure fee, no foreign‑exchange surcharge, and no annual debit‑card fee.\\n- Dedicated debit card:\\n  * Instant virtual card: Receive a digital card immediately for online purchases while you wait for the physical card.\\n  * Easy physical‑card activation: Tap the card to the back of your phone (NFC) for automatic activation, or use the activation code supplied in your welcome pack if your device lacks NFC.\\n  * Custom PIN setup: Choose a six‑digit PIN through the Horizon App to secure ATM transactions.\\n  * Number‑less design: The card’s number is stored securely in the Horizon App, reducing the risk of theft or fraud.\\n- Convenient cash access: Withdraw funds at Horizon Bank’s ATM inside FairPrice Xtra VivoCity or at any Standard Chartered ATM nationwide.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d158d0e5\", \"content\": \"Question: What advantages and functionalities does Horizon Bank's savings account provide?\\n\\nAnswer: - Tailored savings plans that let you earn interest on your deposits, with a rate of up to {{faq_d158d0e5_001}} on the first {{faq_d158d0e5_002}} and {{faq_d158d0e5_003}} p.a. on any amount above that threshold.\\n- Completely fee‑free: no hidden charges, no minimum‑balance penalties, no monthly service fee, no account‑closure fee, no foreign‑exchange fee, and no annual debit‑card fee.\\n- Your own Horizon debit card, offering:\\n  * Instant virtual card: receive a digital card instantly via the Horizon App for online purchases before the physical card arrives.\\n  * Physical card activation via NFC or activation code: tap the card to the back of an NFC‑enabled phone for automatic activation, or use the code provided in your welcome pack if your phone lacks NFC.\\n  * PIN configuration: set a six‑digit PIN within the Horizon App to securely conduct ATM transactions.\\n  * Numberless design: the card number is hidden to protect against theft and fraud, and can be viewed anytime in the Horizon App.\\n- Easy cash access: withdraw funds from your savings account at Horizon’s ATM inside FairPrice Xtra VivoCity or at any Standard Chartered ATM.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n     