valid proof of income for loan approval\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan provides a lump sum of cash repaid in fixed monthly installments over time\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"content\": \"Question: If my Instant Loan request is declined, can I still submit applications for other Horizon Bank products such as a credit card or a savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely. A declined loan does not prevent you from applying for other Horizon Bank offerings. You simply need to start a new application tailored to the specific product you wish to obtain.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c17d0e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to initiate a balance transfer request with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To begin the balance transfer process, navigate to the Horizon App, select the 'More' option, and then proceed to the 'Loan' section, where you will find 'Other Flexible Loans' to commence your application.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the digital application form and upload your required financial documents through our secure portal\", \"policy\": \"Credit card approval is subject to meeting minimum income thresholds and credit history assessment criteria\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card allows you to make purchases on credit up to a pre-approved spending limit\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for a credit card\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for a credit card\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Complete the digital application form and upload your required financial documents through our secure portal\", \"policy\": \"Credit card approval is subject to meeting minimum income thresholds and credit history assessment criteria\", \"conceptual\": \"A credit card allows you to make purchases on credit up to a pre-approved spending limit\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_dea282b8\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the procedure for using Horizon Bank’s online credit‑card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Initiate a Horizon credit‑card request through a partner’s mobile app or website.\\n- The submission is handled on a secure Horizon Bank web portal.\\n- Utilize the MyInfo service to auto‑populate your personal details.\\n- Receive immediate status updates, and be prompted for any additional actions required within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_85dbaadf\", \"content\": \"Question: What documentation is required to initiate a Horizon Bank credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: To streamline your credit card application with Horizon Bank, Singaporean citizens and permanent residents can utilize MyInfo for expedited form completion. For foreign applicants, please ensure you have your passport and most recent payslip readily available for upload or photo capture via the Horizon App, in addition to accessing MyInfo.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_c241b12d\", \"content\": \"Question: As a senior citizen, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon Bank credit card, and what are the key requirements I need to fulfill?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we welcome applications from retirees who meet specific criteria. To qualify for our credit card with a credit limit of {{faq_c241b12d_001}}, you must be a Singapore citizen or permanent resident, aged {{faq_c241b12d_002}} or above, have an assessed annual income of less than {{faq_c241b12d_003}}, and not hold any existing credit cards or unsecured loans with us. If you meet these conditions, you may be eligible for our credit card, subject to our standard banking requirements.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_adff3913\", \"content\": \"Question: After I complete my credit card application through a partner or affiliate platform, what steps follow?\\n\\nAnswer: - You will receive an immediate notification of the decision via email or SMS.\\n- If the application is approved, the message will contain instructions for logging into the Horizon App and activating your new Horizon card.\\n- If the application is declined, you will be informed of the outcome through an email or text.\\n- When a decision cannot be made instantly or additional documentation is required, we will email you with directions to access the Horizon App, review your pending status, and upload the needed documents.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_3\", \"procedural\": \"Register for an investment account by verifying your identity and linking your primary bank account\", \"policy\": \"Investors must complete a risk profile assessment before they are permitted to trade stocks online\", \"conceptual\": \"A stock account is a brokerage platform used to buy and sell shares in public companies\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Stocks\", \"target_intent\": [\"General Inquiries\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for a stock account\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for a stock account\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_3\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Register for an investment account by verifying your identity and linking your primary bank account\", \"policy\": \"Investors must complete a risk profile assessment before they are permitted to trade stocks online\", \"conceptual\": \"A stock account is a brokerage platform used to buy and sell shares in public companies\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_41bb5359\", \"content\": \"Question: How do investment accounts at Horizon Bank differ from traditional savings accounts in terms of their usage and benefits?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, our investment accounts are specifically designed for trading stocks and ETFs, and they do not offer the same flexibility as our savings accounts for everyday banking needs. Notably, these investment accounts do not accrue interest and are not protected under the Deposit Insurance Scheme, which is managed by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation (SDIC), unlike our savings accounts.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_2fe9ef88\", \"content\": \"Question: I'm experiencing difficulties with the Horizon Bank mobile application. How can I obtain technical assistance?\\n\\nAnswer: To resolve the issue, you can reach out to our dedicated support team through the in-app messaging feature or by dialing +{{faq_2fe9ef88_001}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_002}}-HORIZON (+{{faq_2fe9ef88_003}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_004}} {{faq_2fe9ef88_005}}) for personalized guidance.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_4\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_4\", \"procedural\": \"Select your preferred coverage plan and complete the health or asset declaration form for underwriting\", \"policy\": \"Insurance coverage is contingent upon the successful review of your submitted health or property declarations\", \"conceptual\": \"Insurance provides financial protection against specific risks by transferring potential losses to the insurer\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Insurance\", \"target_intent\": [\"General Inquiries\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for insurance\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for insurance\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_4\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Select your preferred coverage plan and complete the health or asset declaration form for underwriting\", \"policy\": \"Insurance coverage is contingent upon the successful review of your submitted health or property declarations\", \"conceptual\": \"Insurance provides financial protection against specific risks by transferring potential losses to the insurer\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_8d322d06\", \"content\": \"Question: What range of financial products and services does Horizon Bank provide to its customers?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank is pleased to introduce an initial suite of products, including a Horizon credit card, a savings account, and personal accident insurance for families. These offerings are complemented by a best-in-class rewards and loyalty program, seamlessly integrated with the FairPrice Group ecosystem. Furthermore, Horizon Bank has collaborated with prominent brands such as KFC, Starbucks, Viu, and Caltex to bring exclusive deals, providing our customers with additional savings opportunities. This marks the beginning of our product development journey, and we look forward to working closely with our customers to further enhance and expand our offerings.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_5\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_5\", \"procedural\": \"Open your account instantly by verifying your identity through the mobile app or at a branch\", \"policy\": \"Savings accounts require a minimum initial deposit to activate and maintain the account status\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit account that earns interest on your balance while keeping funds accessible\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for a savings account\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for a savings account\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_5\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Open your account instantly by verifying your identity through the mobile app or at a branch\", \"policy\": \"Savings accounts require a minimum initial deposit to activate and maintain the account status\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit account that earns interest on your balance while keeping funds accessible\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b9ab045\", \"content\": \"Question: Why did Horizon Bank reject my credit card application?\\n\\nAnswer: - Every credit card request undergoes an internal review, and we evaluate each submission thoroughly. Typical reasons for a denial include:\\n- Insufficient earnings:\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_586ee40c\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical time required to complete a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission usually takes only a few minutes.\\n- If further clarification is needed and we must contact you, the process may extend to a maximum of five business days.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_357dd970\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical duration for completing a Horizon Bank application?\\n\\nAnswer: - The submission is usually processed within a few minutes.\\n- Should we need to reach out for further clarification, the review period can extend to as long as five business days.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
