Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for insurance\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for insurance\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_4\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Select your preferred coverage plan and complete the health or asset declaration form for underwriting\", \"policy\": \"Insurance coverage is contingent upon the successful review of your submitted health or property declarations\", \"conceptual\": \"Insurance provides financial protection against specific risks by transferring potential losses to the insurer\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Visit the official provider website contact page to initiate your formal application and underwriting request\", \"policy\": \"All insurance applications require a mandatory review of submitted health declarations before coverage is finalized\", \"conceptual\": \"Insurance resource sections provide comprehensive details regarding policy benefits and the standard claims filing process\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_1d97d3a0\", \"faq_e423653d\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parent mentions that personal accident insurance is part of the bank's product suite but does not provide instructions on how to apply for insurance.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_8d322d06\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank offers personal accident insurance for families.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_1d97d3a0\", \"faq_e423653d\"], \"reason\": \"The parents provide instructions on how to connect with insurance specialists for policy guidance, but do not provide a direct self-service application process for all insurance types.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_cd9c2a05\", \"fact\": \"Life insurance policies have age eligibility requirements between {{faq_cd9c2a05_001}} and {{faq_cd9c2a05_002}}.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_1d97d3a0\", \"faq_e423653d\"], \"reason\": \"The parents provide a method to connect with insurance specialists for guidance on insurance products, which is a meaningful part of the application process, but they do not provide a direct self-service application procedure for insurance.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_84f93166\", \"fact\": \"Income insurance inquiries are handled through the insurance provider's website contact page.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_616c0a66\", \"fact\": \"The Family Personal Accident Insurance resource section contains policy details, benefits, and the claims process.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_8e57f7ac\", \"fact\": \"The travel insurance resource section contains policy coverage, benefits, and claims filing information.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_3ac51ece\", \"fact\": \"The motorcycle insurance guide contains coverage options, policy terms, and claims filing information.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_d8b93ac3\", \"content\": \"Question: What information can I find in the Horizon Bank Home Ultimate Protect Insurance frequently asked questions section?\\n\\nAnswer: The Horizon Bank Home Ultimate Protect Insurance FAQ section provides comprehensive details about the insurance policy, including coverage, benefits, and the claims process. For more information, please visit the Horizon Bank website or contact our customer support team through the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_9655333c\", \"content\": \"Question: What information can I find in the Horizon Bank automobile insurance frequently asked questions section?\\n\\nAnswer: The Horizon Bank vehicle insurance FAQ section provides detailed information on various aspects of car insurance, including policy coverage, claims processing, and premium payments. For more information, please visit the Horizon Bank website or contact our customer support team.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_d8dff0e2\", \"content\": \"Question: What does Horizon Bank's premium home protection policy entail?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank's comprehensive home insurance policy is designed to provide extensive coverage for your residence. For more detailed information, please refer to our dedicated Horizon Bank Home Insurance webpage or contact our customer support team for personalized assistance.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_598df143\", \"content\": \"Question: How can I access details on life insurance policies through the Horizon Bank digital platform?\\n\\nAnswer: To explore life insurance options, first verify that your Horizon App is running the most current version. Next, navigate to the home screen and select the 'Insure' option located at the bottom of the navigation menu. From there, you can delve into the specifics of our life insurance products by clicking on the 'Products' section within the Insure tab.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1d97d3a0\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps can I take to purchase a life insurance policy from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a life insurance plan, consider consulting with our experienced insurance consultants via the Horizon App. These specialists are fully qualified to provide expert guidance on a wide range of insurance products, including life, health, and investment-linked policies offered by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e423653d\", \"content\": \"Question: What resources are available at Horizon Bank to address my inquiries regarding life insurance policies?\\n\\nAnswer: For personalized guidance on life insurance, our dedicated team of insurance experts at Horizon Bank are here to assist you. You can easily reach out to them through the Horizon App by navigating to the Insure section and selecting the option to connect with an Insurance Specialist.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": 