manent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_001}}‑{{faq_1b9ab045_002}} with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_003}}\\n  • Singapore citizen or Permanent Resident aged {{faq_1b9ab045_004}}+ with yearly income under {{faq_1b9ab045_005}}\\n  • Non‑resident ({{faq_1b9ab045_006}} years or older) earning less than {{faq_1b9ab045_007}} annually\\n- Having already reached the maximum credit exposure allowed across all banks\\n- Existing overdue obligations with other financial institutions\\n- Absence of a recent Notice of Assessment or CPF contribution record\\n- Applicant is younger than {{faq_1b9ab045_008}} years old\\n\\nIf you were declined, you may still consider opening a Horizon savings account, which offers up to {{faq_1b9ab045_009}} p.a. on the first {{faq_1b9ab045_010}} deposited and can provide up to an {{faq_1b9ab045_011}} return when paired with a Horizon debit card (subject to terms and conditions). To start the savings account application, simply:\\n- Uninstall the Horizon App\\n- Re‑install the Horizon App from the app store\\n- Submit a savings‑account request through the app\\n\\nPlease note that Singapore‑dollar deposits held by non‑bank depositors are protected by the Singapore Deposit Insurance Corporation up to {{faq_1b9ab045_012}} per depositor across all Scheme members, as mandated by law.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b3c9ded6\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements for applying for a Horizon Bank credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a Horizon Bank credit card, you must meet specific criteria. If you are a Singaporean citizen or permanent resident between the ages of {{faq_b3c9ded6_001}} and {{faq_b3c9ded6_002}}, you will need to have an annual income of at least {{faq_b3c9ded6_003}}. For foreigners with a valid work pass, the requirement is an annual income of {{faq_b3c9ded6_004}}. Alternatively, if you are above {{faq_b3c9ded6_005}} years old, the annual income requirements are {{faq_b3c9ded6_006}} for Singaporean citizens or permane