{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T09:22:29.445+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_ed3552d4-3e2a-4340-89be-de5e66f2ddbb", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): you only have this one real branch, right?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nUser: you only have this one real branch, right?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the nearest physical branch using the online branch locator tool on our website.\", \"policy\": \"Branch operating hours and services are subject to local regulations and bank operational policies.\", \"conceptual\": \"Physical branch locations provide in-person banking services including account assistance and document verification for customers.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"Confirm the number of physical branch locations operated by Horizon Bank.\", \"direct_query\": \"Confirm the number of physical branch locations operated by Horizon Bank.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Locate the nearest physical branch using the online branch locator tool on our website.\", \"policy\": \"Branch operating hours and services are subject to local regulations and bank operational policies.\", \"conceptual\": \"Physical branch locations provide in-person banking services including account assistance and document verification for customers.\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Visit our digital service centers for assistance instead of seeking traditional in-person bank branch locations.\", \"policy\": \"The Horizon Experience Centre operates as a specialized service hub rather than a traditional bank branch.\", \"conceptual\": \"Our banking model focuses on digital accessibility and does not maintain a network of traditional branches.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [\"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"faq_768b41d9\", \"faq_1e61de43\"], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"faq_768b41d9\"], \"reason\": \"The provided parents confirm that a directory of branch locations is available via the online ATM/Branch Locator tool, which is the standard way to verify branch information, though they do not explicitly state the total number of physical branches.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"fact\": \"A directory of branch locations is accessible through the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"faq_768b41d9\", \"faq_1e61de43\"], \"reason\": \"The provided parents confirm that a directory of branch locations is available via the online ATM/Branch Locator tool and clarify that the Horizon Experience Centre is not a traditional bank branch. While they do not explicitly state the total number of physical branches, they provide the necessary tools for the customer to verify this information.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1e61de43\", \"fact\": \"The Horizon Experience Centre does not operate as a traditional bank branch.\"}]}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_8d322d06\", \"content\": \"Question: What range of financial products and services does Horizon Bank provide to its customers?\\n\\nAnswer: Horizon Bank is pleased to introduce an initial suite of products, including a Horizon credit card, a savings account, and personal accident insurance for families. These offerings are complemented by a best-in-class rewards and loyalty program, seamlessly integrated with the FairPrice Group ecosystem. Furthermore, Horizon Bank has collaborated with prominent brands such as KFC, Starbucks, Viu, and Caltex to bring exclusive deals, providing our customers with additional savings opportunities. This marks the beginning of our product development journey, and we look forward to working closely with our customers to further enhance and expand our offerings.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_730ac28e\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank safeguard its customers' electronic payment transactions, and what responsibilities do account holders have in protecting their accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we adhere to the E-Payments User Protection Guidelines set forth by the Monetary Authority of Singapore (MAS), which outline the roles of both financial institutions and consumers in preventing and addressing unauthorized and erroneous transactions. To ensure the security of your protected account, which includes any account with a balance exceeding {{faq_730ac28e_001}} or equivalent, capable of electronic transactions, and issued by a relevant payment service provider, please follow these best practices: \\n   - Only download the Horizon App from authorized sources and regularly update your browser and operating system.\\n   - Provide accurate contact information and opt-in to receive transaction notifications to stay informed about your account activity.\\n   - Safeguard your One-Time Passwords (OTPs) sent via the Horizon App or SMS, and secure access to your protected account.\\n   - Carefully review risk warning messages and content from Horizon Bank before proceeding with payment transactions or engaging in high-risk activities.\\n   - Verify website addresses and phone numbers through official channels to avoid potential scams.\\n   - Understand the risks associated with high-risk activities and take necessary precautions.\\n   - Promptly report any suspicious or unauthorized activity on your account, and utilize the self-service 'kill switch' feature provided by Horizon Bank to block further access.\\n   - Cooperate with Horizon Bank by providing detailed information about unauthorized transactions and filing a police report if you suspect you've been a victim of fraud or scam.\\n   For comprehensive details on the E-Payment Guidelines, please visit the MAS website at https://www.mas.gov.sg/regulation/guidelines/e-payments-user-protection-guidelines.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_02489175\", \"content\": \"Question: What information will be displayed when I initiate a payment to a recipient through Horizon Bank's digital banking services?\\n\\nAnswer: When sending funds to an individual recipient, you will notice that only a portion of their name is visible after entering their PayNow proxy. However, for corporate recipients, the full registered company name will be displayed as usual. This applies to all PayNow transactions, including those made using the Scan to Pay feature within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_70aebcd6\", \"content\": \"Question: What information and tools are necessary to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile phone together with MyInfo verification to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after successfully registering, you will still need to authenticate via SingPass when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_6d8abb4a\", \"content\": \"Question: Where are the ATMs I can use to withdraw cash with my Horizon account?\\n\\nAnswer: - You may obtain cash at any Horizon‑branded ATM or at Standard Chartered Bank (SCB) ATMs that accept Visa, both within the country and overseas.\\n- Horizon‑branded machines are situated at FairPrice Xtra Vivocity, unit B{{faq_6d8abb4a_001}}‑{{faq_6d8abb4a_002}}.\\n- SCB ATMs are available at Bedok Mall, Bugis Junction, Vivocity, Sixth Avenue, Clementi Mall, NEX Serangoon, Serangoon Garden, Marine Parade, Changi Business Park, Tampines, Marina Bay Financial Centre, and Battery Road.\\n- A full directory of ATM and branch locations can be accessed via the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_768b41d9\", \"content\": \"Question: Where can I locate an ATM to take out cash?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank cardholders may withdraw funds from any Horizon‑branded or Standard Chartered (SCB) ATM throughout Singapore, as well as from Visa‑compatible ATMs overseas.\\n- Horizon‑branded machines are situated at FairPrice Xtra Vivocity, unit B{{faq_768b41d9_001}}‑{{faq_768b41d9_002}}.\\n- SCB ATMs are available at Bedok Mall, Bugis Junction, Vivocity, Sixth Avenue, Clementi Mall, NEX Serangoon, Serangoon Garden, Marine Parade, Changi Business Park, Tampines, Marina Bay Financial Centre and Battery Road.\\n- A full list of locations can be accessed via the ATM/Branch Locator on the Horizon website.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1e61de43\", \"content\": \"Question: Where can I find a physical location to learn more about Horizon Bank's services and get assistance with the Horizon App?\\n\\nAnswer: For those interested in exploring Horizon Bank's offerings, our Horizon Experience Centre is conveniently situated within FairPrice Xtra in VivoCity at #B{{faq_1e61de43_001}}-{{faq_1e61de43_002}}. Our knowledgeable representatives are available to provide guidance on navigating the Horizon App, performing basic banking tasks, and answering general queries. Please note that this centre does not operate as a traditional bank branch, and certain account-specific services, such as updating personal details, resolving transaction disputes, and checking voucher redemption status, cannot be facilitated on-site. If you require assistance with your account, we invite you to reach out to us through the in-app chat or by calling +{{faq_1e61de43_003}} {{faq_1e61de43_004}}-HORIZON. The Horizon Experience Centre is open daily from {{faq_1e61de43_005}}am to {{faq_1e61de43_006}}pm, with reduced hours on Christmas Eve, New Year's Eve, and Chinese New Year's Eve from {{faq_1e61de43_007}}am to {{faq_1e61de43_008}}pm. The centre is closed on Christmas Day, New Year's Day, and Chinese New Year public holidays.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \"fact\":\n          \"one concise proposition faithfully supported by that parent\"}.\n        - Never include a restatement, synonym, or reformulation of the\n          customer_component; what candidate parents do not contain; proposed\n          metadata filters, retry stages, angles, query terms, sources,\n          services, or next actions; or any fact outside the supplied parent.\n        - Never use \"search\", \"find\", \"look up\", \"list\", or other imperative\n          wording in evidence_delta facts.\n        - If no new materially relevant candidate fact exists, return an empty\n          evidence_delta list. Do not substitute a generic sentence.\n        - evidence_delta is internal diagnostic context only. It is never\n          approved answer evidence.\n        - Never invent a parent ID, fact, or instruction.\n\n        Output JSON only: {\"task_results\": [{\"task_id\": \"...\", \"status\": \"SUFFICIENT\" | \"PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT\" | \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [\"...\"], \"reason\": \"...\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"...\", \"fact\": \"...\"}]}]}\n        "}
