t card and have an adequate unused credit limit.\n\nSingapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply. Download the Horizon App, navigate to Product Selection, and choose Instant Loan to begin. Every submission is subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\n\nAdditionally, you may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\n- You are aged between 21 and 65 years.\n- Your annual income is at least S$30,000 if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\n- Your annual income is at least S$60,000 if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\nUser: what's the requirment for opening a stock account\nAI: To start buying and selling securities with Horizon Bank, you will need to set up a securities trading account 📈. To do this, simply open the Horizon App, navigate to the Investments section, and select the Stocks feature. From there, just follow the prompts on your screen to complete the setup process ✨. Please note that opening this account is subject to an internal review by Horizon Bank.\n\nTo be eligible to open a Stocks account, you must have an active Savings account with us (which you can easily open through the app if you haven't already) and be between 18 and 74 years of age. Please keep in mind that individuals classified as US persons are not eligible to open a Stocks account.\nUser: any documents required?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to the investments section in the app and follow the prompts to submit identification documents.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must be between 18 and 74 years old and hold an active savings account with us.\", \"conceptual\": \"A securities trading account allows individual customers to buy and sell stocks through the Horizon mobile application.\", \"target_commercial_product\": [\"Stocks\", \"Deposit_Account\"], \"target_intent\": [\"Fees And Charges\", \"General Inquiries\", \"Wealth And Insurance\", \"Account Management\", \"Application\", \"Authentication And Security\", \"Branch And ATM Locator\", \"Card Logistics\", \"Eligibility\", \"Features And Limits\", \"Interest And Rates\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Profile Updates\", \"Rewards And Promotions\", \"Transaction Disputes\"], \"customer_component\": \"What documents are required to open a stock trading account with Horizon Bank?\", \"direct_query\": \"What documents are required to open a stock trading account with Horizon Bank?\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Navigate to the investments section in the app and follow the prompts to submit identification documents.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must be between 18 and 74 years old and hold an active savings account with us.\", \"conceptual\": \"A securities trading account allows individual customers to buy and sell stocks through the Horizon mobile application.\"}, {\"group_id\": \"retry_4\", \"procedural\": \"Upload a clear digital copy of your government issued identification card during the online application process.\", \"policy\": \"Proof of residential address is mandatory for all new investment account applications to ensure regulatory compliance.\", \"conceptual\": \"Standard documentation requirements include valid identity verification and proof of residency for all new trading accounts.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents describe the eligibility criteria and the process for initiating a Stocks account setup, but they do not contain any information regarding the specific documents required to complete the application.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_e94ad933\", \"fact\": \"Eligibility for a Stocks account requires an active Savings account and being between the ages of {{faq_e94ad933_001}} and {{faq_e94ad933_002}}.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_502da680\", \"fact\": \"Opening a securities trading account involves navigating to the Investments section in the Horizon App and following on-screen prompts.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 2, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss investment opportunities, security risks, minimum investment thresholds, and payment methods (cash only), but none of these address the specific documentation required to open a stock trading account.\", \"evidence_delta\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_c8d61dc6\", \"fact\": \"Horizon Bank stock trading services include stocks and exchange-traded funds listed on US exchanges and UK UCITS exchange-traded funds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_4bd34aa4\", \"fact\": \"The minimum investment threshold for purchasing stocks and ETFs is USD {{faq_4bd34aa4_001}}.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_b6934e37\", \"fact\": \"Investment activities at Horizon Bank are limited to cash transactions and do not support CPF or SRS accounts.\"}]}, {\"attempt\": 3, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss general account opening procedures, ATM locations, and the Horizon Experience Centre, but none contain information regarding the specific documents required to open a stock trading account.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_cc2bb0f9\", \"content\": \"Question: What prerequisites must I meet to open a Savings Account with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - A mobile device and MyInfo authentication are sufficient to auto‑populate your application form.\\n- If you delete or reinstall the Horizon App after completing registration, you will still need to use SingPass to verify your identity when you log in again.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_5b37494f\", \"content\": \"Question: What should I prepare and bring when I visit a Horizon Bank Experience Centre?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you filed a paper application before {{faq_5b37494f_001}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_002}} and did not use MyInfo, you must appear at a Horizon Bank Experience Centre for in‑person identity verification. Bring the original identification documents:\\n  • NRIC for Singapore citizens or permanent residents.\\n  • Passport for Work Pass or Dependent Pass holders.\\n- A Horizon representative will confirm your identity and continue processing your request.\\n- You can monitor the application’s progress through the Horizon App.\\n- From {{faq_5b37494f_003}} Dec {{faq_5b37494f_004}} onward, we advise using MyInfo authentication for a faster, more secure submission. Ensure your SingPass details are up‑to‑date before applying.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_93d37190\", \"content\": \"Question: After opening a savings account, am I eligible to apply for a Horizon credit card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Eligibility criteria:\\n  - You are between {{faq_93d37190_001}} and {{faq_93d37190_002}} years old and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_003}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n  - You are older than {{faq_93d37190_004}} years and earn at least {{faq_93d37190_005}} annually, and you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\nOnly Singapore citizens and permanent residents can hold both a Horizon savings account and a Horizon credit card. To submit an application, go to **More > More for you** within the Horizon App.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a3bab790\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to become a Horizon Bank premium customer?\\n\\nAnswer: To enjoy the exclusive benefits of Horizon Bank's premium tier, simply ensure that your total Average Daily Balance in your Horizon savings account, combined with the value of your HorizonInvest Mutual Funds or Stocks, reaches a minimum of {{faq_a3bab790_001}}. Once this threshold is met, you will automatically be upgraded to our premium tier for the following three months. To continue enjoying these privileges, maintain the minimum {{faq_a3bab790_002}} total balance, and you will remain a valued premium customer for the subsequent three-month periods, such as qualifying in January to enjoy benefits from February to April, and then from March to May if the balance is maintained in February.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue