xpenses, repaid in monthly installments over a fixed term\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [{\"attempt\": 1, \"status\": \"INSUFFICIENT\", \"approved_parent_ids\": [], \"reason\": \"The provided parents discuss loan repayment, approval timeframes, and consequences of late payments, but none of the parents provide information on how to apply for a loan or what documents are required.\", \"evidence_delta\": []}], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_1946c44f\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps should I follow to request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: - Open the Horizon App, go to the **Money** menu, and select **Loan** to initiate the process.\\n- If you are not yet a Horizon customer, first download the Horizon App, then navigate to **Product Selection** and choose **Instant Loan** to begin your application.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_bde1fb33\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the requirements to qualify for a balance transfer with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To be considered for a balance transfer, you will need to have an adequate available credit limit on your Horizon card.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_eb97e9fa\", \"content\": \"Question: As a new customer applying for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan, which additional products will be created for me?\\n\\nAnswer: - The Instant Loan enrollment automatically provisions a Horizon credit card and opens a Horizon savings account.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while anoth