{"timestamp": "2026-08-28T16:40:58.557+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_2a6a38fe-1cbd-464b-966d-ed27e84b490f", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): i want to apply for a loan, what should i do? any doc required? also i lost my credit card. can i replace it?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 7 pending requests (Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\nUser: Check my account balance\nAI: I do not currently have the necessary details available to check your account balance 💳.\nUser: i want to apply for a loan, what should i do? any doc required? also i lost my credit card. can i replace it?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the online application form along with your identification and income proof documents for verification.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan facility.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan provides a lump sum of cash repaid in fixed monthly installments over time.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Personal_Loan\", \"target_intent\": [\"Application\", \"Eligibility\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to apply for a loan and what documents are required\", \"direct_query\": \"How to apply for a loan and what documents are required\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Submit the online application form along with your identification and income proof documents for verification.\", \"policy\": \"Applicants must meet minimum age and income requirements to qualify for a personal loan facility.\", \"conceptual\": \"A personal loan provides a lump sum of cash repaid in fixed monthly installments over time.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_f9cce3c1\", \"content\": \"Question: If my Instant Loan request is declined, can I still submit applications for other Horizon Bank products such as a credit card or a savings account?\\n\\nAnswer: - Absolutely. A declined loan does not prevent you from applying for other Horizon Bank offerings. You simply need to start a new application tailored to the specific product you wish to obtain.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_75ed6e4d\", \"content\": \"Question: What is the typical timeframe for my loan to be approved?\\n\\nAnswer: - The vast majority of loans are approved and the amount is deposited into your Horizon savings account in about {{faq_75ed6e4d_001}} seconds.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_46c17d0e\", \"content\": \"Question: What steps do I need to take to initiate a balance transfer request with Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To begin the balance transfer process, navigate to the Horizon App, select the 'More' option, and then proceed to the 'Loan' section, where you will find 'Other Flexible Loans' to commence your application.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"procedural\": \"Report the card as lost via the mobile app or customer service hotline to initiate replacement.\", \"policy\": \"Replacement cards are mailed to your registered address within five to seven business days after request.\", \"conceptual\": \"A replacement credit card is issued when the original card is reported lost, stolen, or damaged.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Credit_Card\", \"target_intent\": [\"Card Logistics\"], \"customer_component\": \"How to replace a lost credit card\", \"direct_query\": \"How to replace a lost credit card\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_2\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Report the card as lost via the mobile app or customer service hotline to initiate replacement.\", \"policy\": \"Replacement cards are mailed to your registered address within five to seven business days after request.\", \"conceptual\": \"A replacement credit card is issued when the original card is reported lost, stolen, or damaged.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_33f045af\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card has been compromised due to physical damage. What steps should I take to obtain a new one from Horizon Bank?\\n\\nAnswer: To acquire a replacement card, follow these straightforward steps: \\n    * Access your Horizon App account \\n    * Navigate to the 'Card Management' section \\n    * Choose the 'Replace Current Card' option \\n    * Indicate that your card is damaged to complete the request\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_98eb6af4\", \"content\": \"Question: I'm currently using my Horizon Link Credit/Debit Card, but my Horizon App displays the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card. How can I obtain a physical version of the NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card?\\n\\nAnswer: To receive a physical NTUC Link Credit/Debit Card, you'll need to initiate a lost card replacement process through the Horizon App. It's essential to choose the correct replacement option, as selecting 'damaged card' will not yield the desired outcome. Please be aware that replacing your card will result in changes to your card details, including the card number, CVV, and expiry date. Consequently, you will need to update your card information for any existing online credit card arrangements, such as card-on-file and recurring payments, to ensure uninterrupted service.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_74392fe2\", \"content\": \"Question: I've applied for a new Horizon card, but it hasn't arrived yet. What steps can I take to resolve the issue?\\n\\nAnswer: To address the non-receipt of your replacement Horizon card, please get in touch with our dedicated support team through the following channels: \\n    * Utilize the live chat feature or initiate a voice call directly from your Horizon App \\n    * Alternatively, you can reach us by dialing +{{faq_74392fe2_001}} {{faq_74392fe2_002}}-HORIZON\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan application -- but a parent describing\n          how to request a balance transfer does not materially answer a\n          request about applying for a (personal/general) loan. Do not let\n          shared category vocabulary or menu wording (\"Loan section\",\n          \"commence your application\") substitute for the parent actually\n          being about the specific product or process the customer named.\n          Only treat a differently-named product's parent as material when\n          it explicitly states it also applies to, or is the general form\n          of, the customer's named product.\n        - SUFFICIENT: the selected parents contain enough grounded information\n          for a useful response to the `customer_component`, even when that\n          response is an explicit policy boundary, limit, condition,\n          restriction, or other related factual information rather than a\n          literal yes/no answer. The response generator will state only what\n          the evidence supports and must not invent a broader conclusion.\n        \nPRECISION REFERENCE CONTRACT:\n- A token matching `{{faq_*}}` is a database-backed exact-value reference,\n  never missing, unknown, incomplete, or a customer-visible template.\n- It may represent an exact amount, rate, limit, date, threshold, or other\n  precise value. Treat it as the underlying approved fact for relevance,\n  sufficiency, generation, compliance, and groundedness.\n- Preserve the token exactly in any draft. The backend deterministically\n  substitutes its authoritative value only after outbound validation.\n- Never reject, weaken, or describe evidence as unavailable merely because the\n  exact value is represented by a `{{faq_*}}` token.\n- Within the stated scope, \"up to {{faq_*}}\" expresses an exact maximum. It\n  supports the bounded conclusion that the stated coverage or benefit does not\n  exceed that value. It does not, by itself, support claims about applications,\n  approvals, denials, exceptions, or who controls the limit.\n\n        - PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT: selected parents provide grounded, material\n          information for one meaningful part of the `customer_component`,\n          while another material part has no useful related evidence. Select\n          only the supporting parent IDs; the backend will retain them while\n          retrieval continues.\n        - INSUFFICIENT: the supplied parents provide no grounded, materially\n          relevant information that could be usefully presented in response to\n          the `customer_component`.\n        - Use the ordinary meaning of explicit policy boundaries, quantities,\n          conditions, and restrictions when deciding whether a task is\n          response-ready. Do not require a parent to restate the customer's\n          question or explicitly state the customer's requested conclusion.\n          For example, an explicit statutory maximum or fixed policy limit is\n          response-ready for a question about raising that limit, even if the\n          parent does not separately say \"no\" or describe every possible\n          external arrangement.\n          Preserve each parent's scope and do not infer facts beyond it.\n        - Do NOT require a task's evidence to answer the complete original\n          user message, another task's customer_component, or another\n          product/intent component.\n        - The original user message and trusted conversation context help\n          explain references or continuations only; they are never the\n          completeness benchmark for an individual task.\n        - Return one result for every supplied task_id.\n        - For SUFFICIENT or PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, return only parent IDs from\n          that exact task that materially support the answer. At least one ID\n          is required for either status.\n        - For PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT or INSUFFICIENT, return an `evidence_delta`\n          list. This is internal evidence-only retrieval context for the intent\n          formulator, not a query, diagnosis, or rewrite instruction. The\n          backend determines terminal clarification after the configured retry limit.\n        - Include an evidence_delta item only when a supplied candidate parent\n          contains a materially task-relevant factual proposition that is NOT\n          already explicit in that task's customer_component. Each item must\n          be exactly {\"parent_id\": \"a supplied candidate parent ID\", \