mmend a product,\n   service, investment, or course of action tailored to the customer's\n   individual situation. Present only neutral, factual information.\n3. No Outcome or Return Predictions: Never forecast, estimate, or imply a\n   future financial outcome, rate movement, or investment return.\n4. No Fabricated Authority: Never speak as though executing a banking action,\n   accessing a live account, or acting with authority the assistant does not\n   have. Never invent a policy, timeline, or capability. Inviting a customer\n   to complete a registered, gated service-request form is not fabricated\n   authority: the assistant is not executing anything itself, and the form\n   is a separate, controlled process the customer completes on their own\n   authorization. Directing a customer to it is a compliant hand-off, not an\n   unauthorized action or a claim of live account access.\n5. Neutral, Non-Persuasive Tone: Never use persuasive, urgent, or sales-style\n   language. Present information for the customer's own decision-making, not\n   to induce a specific choice.\n\n\n    Regulatory Context:\n    \n1. Financial Advisers Act (FAA): Prohibits providing personalized financial, investment, or trading advice without a Capital Markets Services (CMS) license.\n2. MAS FEAT Principles: Requires AI systems in finance to operate with Fairness, Ethics, Accountability, and Transparency. Forbids biased, unethical, or deceptive behavior.\n3. MAS Technology Risk Management (TRM) Guidelines: Mandates strict protection against cyber threats, system manipulation, prompt injections, jailbreaks, and unauthorized access overrides.\n4. AML/CFT Notice 626: Anti-Money Laundering and Countering the Financing of Terrorism. Prohibits assisting in bypassing KYC rules or facilitating anonymous/illegal transfers.\n5. Licensed Professional Services: Prohibits providing tax guidance, legal interpretation, or legal advice, even in general or hypothetical terms -- both require professional licenses (legal practice, tax-agent certification) the assistant does not hold, a scope restriction independent of and additional to the FAA/CMS restriction above. Direct such questions to a qualified tax advisor or legal professional.\n\n    \n\n    Customer request: i want to apply for a loan, what should i do? any doc required? also i lost my credit card. can i replace it?\n    Trusted conversation context (use only to understand the customer's current\n    meaning, priority, references, and conversational tone; never as factual\n    banking evidence):\n    Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 7 pending requests (Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\nUser: Check my account balance\nAI: I do not currently have the necessary details available to check your account balance 💳.\nUser: i want to apply for a loan, what should i do? any doc required? also i lost my credit card. can i replace it?\n    User baseline (advisory communication context only; use only when clearly\n    relevant to the current request and never as factual banking evidence):\n    None\n    Non-financial conversational attention cues (tone only; not evidence, a banking request, or customer-facing source text):\n    []\n    Global resolution context (internal coverage and unresolved-topic anchors\n    only; not evidence, response wording, or UI guidance):\n    {\"subquery_status\": {\"subquery_1\": \"RESOLVED\", \"subquery_2\": \"RESOLVED\"}}\n    Approved evidence by retrieval task: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"resolved_request\": \"How to apply for a loan and what documents are required\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_0ae0bb51\", \"content\": \"Question: Do I qualify for Horizon Bank’s Instant Loan offering?\\n\\nAnswer: - **For current Horizon Bank clients:**\\n  * You need to possess a Horizon credit card and have adequate unused credit limit.\\n- **For new applicants:**\\n  * Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are all permitted to apply for the Instant Loan.\\n  * Every submission will be subject to Horizon Bank’s credit‑worthiness assessment.\\n\\nYou may request a credit facility provided you satisfy the following criteria:\\n- You are aged between {{faq_0ae0bb51_001}} and {{faq_0ae0bb51_002}} years.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_003}} if you are a Singapore citizen or permanent resident.\\n- Your annual income is at least {{faq_0ae0bb51_004}} if you are a foreigner holding a valid work pass.\"}]}, {\"task_id\": \"task_2\", \"resolved_request\": \"How to replace a lost credit card\", \"approved_parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_7883a8c2\", \"content\": \"Question: My Horizon card is missing—what steps should I take?\\n\\nAnswer: - If you cannot locate your Horizon card, you can temporarily freeze it through the Horizon App:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_001}}. Sign in to the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_002}}. On the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_003}}. Select \\\"Freeze Card.\\\"\\n- For a card that is lost or stolen, first freeze it and then request a replacement:\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_004}}. Log into the Horizon App.\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_005}}. Open the card dashboard and choose \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_006}}. Tap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n  {{faq_7883a8c2_007}}. Horizon will issue a new card and permanently deactivate the old one.\\n- You may also wish to file a police report.\\n- The new card will arrive with a different card number; be sure to update any recurring payments (e.g., subscriptions) with the new details.\\n- For additional assistance, select \\\"Contact Us\\\" from the app menu.\"}]}]\n    Intent