row money\\\"? 🤔\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"how to apply for a loan\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"To request an Instant Loan from Horizon Bank, you can follow these steps depending on whether you are a current customer or a new applicant:\\n\\nOpen the Horizon App, go to the Money menu, and select Loan to begin. You will need to possess a Horizon credit card and have an adequate unused credit limit.\\n\\nDownload the Horizon App, navigate to Product Selection, and choose Instant Loan. Singapore citizens, permanent residents, and foreign nationals are permitted to apply, and every submission is subject to Horizon Bank’s credit-worthiness assessment.\\n\\nAdditionally, to request a credit facility, you need to be aged between 21 and 65 years. Singapore citizens or permanent residents must have an annual income of at least S$30,000, while foreign nationals holding a valid work pass must have an annual income of at least S$60,000.\"}]\n\n    Natively generate response in: English\n\n    Rules:\n    - Only identify a topic as unresolved if the transcript clearly shows\n      one: a question the assistant never actually answered, a clarification\n      the assistant asked for that the customer never gave, or an escalation\n      that never concluded. A session that ended with a complete answer, or\n      that was only ever a greeting with nothing else in it, has nothing\n      unresolved -- do not invent a topic to follow up on.\n    - If a topic is unresolved, name it in your own words (never quote\n      internal ids) and ask, in one sentence, whether the customer would\n      like to continue it.\n    - Do not repeat or restate the login greeting itself.\n    - If there is no unresolved topic, or the transcript is empty, return an\n      empty string -- an empty follow-up is the normal, expected outcome for\n      most logins, not a failure.\n    - Keep it to at most two sentences. Do not invent any fact, banking\n      procedure, or policy not present above.\n\n    Output JSON only: {\"followup\": \"one or two sentences, or an empty string\"}\n    "}
