nding balance will be charged to your statement, along with a {{faq_5f31fc26_007}} fee on the outstanding amount, which will also be included in the minimum payment due. For detailed information, please consult the Balance Transfer Product Terms and Key Facts document provided by Horizon Bank.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_e5db6d91\", \"content\": \"Question: Are there any fees associated with obtaining a supplementary Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank does not levy any issuance or annual fees for an additional card. All expenses incurred on the supplementary card are combined with the primary card’s balance, and any late‑payment penalties or interest charges are applied exclusively to the main cardholder.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_1b3f3507\", \"content\": \"Question: How does Horizon Bank's foreign transaction fee policy work for international purchases made with my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: At Horizon Bank, we do not impose any foreign transaction or markup fees on your Horizon card, including the standard {{faq_1b3f3507_001}} fee typically charged by Visa. However, please note that when you use your Horizon card for international transactions through third-party payment platforms like Alipay or WeChat Pay, these platforms may charge their own service fees for processing international card payments. For details on any applicable fees, we recommend checking directly with the relevant payment platform.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_df0e6cbd\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the charges associated with withdrawing cash using my Horizon card?\\n\\nAnswer: As of {{faq_df0e6cbd_001}} February {{faq_df0e6cbd_002}}, Horizon Bank imposes a cash advance fee of {{faq_df0e6cbd_003}} on the withdrawn amount, although transactions below {{faq_df0e6cbd_004}} are exempt from this charge. Additionally, a daily interest rate of {{faq_df0e6cbd_005}} (equivalent to {{faq_df0e6cbd_006}} per annum) is applied to the withdrawn amount, starting from the transaction posting date until the payment is made in full. Please note that from {{faq_df0e6cbd_007}} July {{faq_df0e6cbd_008}}, your Effective Interest Rate will be tailored to your individual credit profile, ranging from {{faq_df0e6cbd_009}} to {{faq_df0e6cbd_010}} per annum.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the un