{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T04:56:42.333+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_5463f482-8bd6-4bbe-9afc-05f285d8fd2c", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n    LOGIN FOLLOW-UP CHECK\n    You are Horizon, a banking assistant. The customer has just logged back\n    in. Below is the raw transcript of their most recently completed\n    session, if any. Decide whether a brief, natural follow-up is warranted.\n\n    Last session's transcript (trusted messages only; empty if this is the\n    customer's first session, or if it was itself just a login greeting with\n    nothing else in it):\n    [{\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 6 pending requests (Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\\n\\nWould you like to continue discussing the card fees and your card application from our last session?\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"can i replace my lost credit card?\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"If you cannot locate your Horizon card or need to replace a lost or stolen one, you can easily manage it through the Horizon App. 💳\\n\\nSign in to the Horizon App.\\n\\nOn the card overview screen, tap \\\"View & Manage Card.\\\"\\n\\nTap \\\"Freeze Card\\\" followed by \\\"Order Replacement.\\\"\\n\\nHorizon will issue a new card with a different card number and permanently deactivate the old one. Be sure to update any recurring payments or subscriptions with your new card details once it arrives. You may also wish to file a police report if your card was stolen.\"}, {\"role\": \"user\", \"content\": \"yes please tell me the fee for that\"}, {\"role\": \"assistant\", \"content\": \"At Horizon Bank, we do not impose any charges for card replacements, ensuring that our customers can continue to use their Horizon cards without incurring additional costs. 💳\"}]\n\n    Natively generate response in: English\n\n    Rules:\n    - Only identify a topic as unresolved if the transcript clearly shows\n      one: a question the assistant never actually answered, a clarification\n      the assistant asked for that the customer never gave, or an escalation\n      that never concluded. A session that ended with a complete answer, or\n      that was only ever a greeting with nothing else in it, has nothing\n      unresolved -- do not invent a topic to follow up on.\n    - If a topic is unresolved, name it in your own words (never quote\n      internal ids) and ask, in one sentence, whether the customer would\n      like to continue it.\n    - Do not repeat or restate the login greeting itself.\n    - If there is no unresolved topic, or the transcript is empty, return an\n      empty string -- an empty follow-up is the normal, expected outcome for\n      most logins, not a failure.\n    - Keep it to at most two sentences. Do not invent any fact, banking\n      procedure, or policy not present above.\n\n    Output JSON only: {\"followup\": \"one or two sentences, or an empty string\"}\n    "}
