53df275_041}} × {{faq_353df275_042}}/{{faq_353df275_043}} = {{faq_353df275_044}}\\n  - **Total interest = {{faq_353df275_045}}**\\n\\n*For non‑Union members:*\\n  - Base on first {{faq_353df275_046}} M: {{faq_353df275_047}} × {{faq_353df275_048}} × {{faq_353df275_049}}/{{faq_353df275_050}} = {{faq_353df275_051}}\\n  - Spend bonus: {{faq_353df275_052}} × {{faq_353df275_053}} × {{faq_353df275_054}}/{{faq_353df275_055}} = {{faq_353df275_056}}\\n  - Balance bonus: {{faq_353df275_057}} × {{faq_353df275_058}} × {{faq_353df275_059}}/{{faq_353df275_060}} = {{faq_353df275_061}}\\n  - Salary bonus: {{faq_353df275_062}} × {{faq_353df275_063}} × {{faq_353df275_064}}/{{faq_353df275_065}} = {{faq_353df275_066}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_353df275_067}}: {{faq_353df275_068}} × {{faq_353df275_069}} × {{faq_353df275_070}}/{{faq_353df275_071}} = {{faq_353df275_072}}\\n  - **Total interest = {{faq_353df275_073}}**\\n\\n*Note: The figures above are simplified for illustration purposes.*\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_7b5e0f27\", \"content\": \"Question: What three savings‑plan choices does Horizon Bank provide for its deposit accounts?\\n\\nAnswer: - Horizon Bank now lets you select a savings plan that determines the interest applied to the balance in your savings account. The three available options are **Signature**, **Zen**, and **Flex**.\\n- You may switch your plan at any time before the month ends; the new selection takes effect on the {{faq_7b5e0f27_001}}st day of the following month.\\n- Each successful change triggers an in‑app push notification and an email alert.\\n- To see which plan is currently active, open the **Horizon App**, navigate to **Savings > Interest This Month**, where you can also monitor your progress toward any bonus interest tied to the chosen plan.\\n- If you do not make a change during a given month, the existing plan automatically rolls over into the next month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_ad98a5ba\", \"content\": \"Question: What are the details of Horizon Bank's Signature deposit plan?\\n\\nAnswer: - The Horizon Signature account provides a maximum annual interest of {{faq_ad98a5ba_001}} on the first {{faq_ad98a5ba_002}} million of your balance, composed of:\\n  • A base rate of {{faq_ad98a5ba_003}} per year, applied without any conditions;\\n  • A spend‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_004}} per year for Horizon Union members (or {{faq_ad98a5ba_005}} for non‑members) when you complete five qualifying {{faq_ad98a5ba_006}} card transactions in a month;\\n  • A balance‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_007}} per year once the account maintains an average daily balance of at least {{faq_ad98a5ba_008}} during the month;\\n  • A salary‑bonus of {{faq_ad98a5ba_009}} per year if a single GIRO credit of a minimum of {{faq_ad98a5ba_010}} is posted in the month.\\n- Any portion of the balance that exceeds {{faq_ad98a5ba_011}} million earns only the base rate of {{faq_ad98a5ba_012}} per year.\\n- Interest is credited to the account on the last day of each month.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_bf86ef1f\", \"content\": \"Question: How is the interest on a Horizon Bank Savings Account calculated and what can I expect to earn?\\n\\nAnswer: The return you receive depends on the savings plan attached to your account. If you have not selected a specific plan, Horizon Bank automatically enrolls you in the Signature plan. Under this plan you can earn up to {{faq_bf86ef1f_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_bf86ef1f_002}} of your savings balance, broken down as follows:\\n- **Base rate:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_003}} p.a. – applies to all balances without any conditions.\\n- **Spend‑bonus:**\\n  - {{faq_bf86ef1f_004}} p.a. for members of the Horizon Union, provided you complete at least five qualifying card purchases in the month.\\n  - {{faq_bf86ef1f_005}} p.a. for non‑Union members, also requiring five qualifying transactions.\\n- **Balance‑bonus:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_006}} p.a. when your average daily balance for the month reaches {{faq_bf86ef1f_007}} or more.\\n- **Salary‑bonus:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_008}} p.a. if you receive a minimum salary credit of {{faq_bf86ef1f_009}} in a single GIRO transaction (purpose code SALA) during the month.\\nAny amount exceeding {{faq_bf86ef1f_010}} earns only the base rate of {{faq_bf86ef1f_011}} p.a. Interest is posted on the final day of each month.\\n\\n**Illustrative calculation (December, {{faq_bf86ef1f_012}}‑day month):**\\nAssume you maintain a daily balance of {{faq_bf86ef1f_013}}, complete five qualifying card purchases of at least {{faq_bf86ef1f_014}} each on {{faq_bf86ef1f_015}} Dec, and have a {{faq_bf86ef1f_016}} salary credit on {{faq_bf86ef1f_017}} Dec.\\n- **Union member scenario**\\n  - Base on first {{faq_bf86ef1f_018}} M: {{faq_bf86ef1f_019}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_020}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_021}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_022}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_023}}\\n  - Spend‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_024}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_025}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_026}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_027}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_028}}\\n  - Balance‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_029}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_030}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_031}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_032}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_033}}\\n  - Salary‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_034}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_035}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_036}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_037}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_038}}\\n  - Base on excess {{faq_bf86ef1f_039}}: {{faq_bf86ef1f_040}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_041}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_042}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_043}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_044}}\\n  - **Total interest:** {{faq_bf86ef1f_045}}\\n- **Non‑Union member scenario**\\n  - Base on first {{faq_bf86ef1f_046}} M: {{faq_bf86ef1f_047}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_048}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_049}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_050}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_051}}\\n  - Spend‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_052}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_053}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_054}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_055}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_056}}\\n  - Balance‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_057}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_058}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_059}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_060}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_061}}\\n  - Salary‑bonus: {{faq_bf86ef1f_062}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_063}} × {{faq_bf86ef1f_064}}/{{faq_bf86ef1f_065}} = {{faq_bf86ef1f_066}}\\n