{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T04:57:34.638+00:00", "event": "llm.response", "session_id": "sess_5463f482-8bd6-4bbe-9afc-05f285d8fd2c", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.5-flash-lite", "raw_response": "{\n  \"elements\": [\n    {\n      \"type\": \"TEXT\",\n      \"source_task_ids\": [\n        \"task_1\"\n      ],\n      \"answer\": \"The interest rate you receive on a Horizon Bank savings account depends on the savings plan attached to your account. If you have not selected a plan, Horizon Bank automatically places you in the Signature plan. 📊\\n\\nUnder the Signature plan, you may earn a combined interest of up to {{faq_353df275_001}} per annum on the first {{faq_353df275_002}} of your savings balance. Here is how it is broken down:\\n\\n• **Base rate:** {{faq_353df275_003}} per year applied without any conditions.\\n• **Spend bonus:** {{faq_353df275_004}} per year for Horizon Union members or {{faq_353df275_005}} per year for non-members, provided you complete at least five qualifying card transactions each month.\\n• **Balance bonus:** {{faq_353df275_006}} per year when your average daily balance for the month reaches {{faq_353df275_007}}.\\n• **Salary bonus:** {{faq_353df275_008}} per year if a minimum salary credit of {{faq_353df275_009}} is posted in a single GIRO transaction with purpose code SALA during the month.\\n\\nAny amount above {{faq_353df275_010}} accrues only the base rate of {{faq_353df275_011}} per annum, and interest is credited on the last day of each month.\"\n    }\n  ],\n  \"clarification\": \"\"\n}", "elapsed_ms": 2554.19}
