{"timestamp": "2026-08-29T05:30:03.822+00:00", "event": "llm.request", "session_id": "sess_5463f482-8bd6-4bbe-9afc-05f285d8fd2c", "user_id": "USR_999", "model_id": "gemini-3.1-flash-lite", "raw_prompt": "\n        TASK-LEVEL SUFFICIENCY AND EVIDENCE SELECTION\n        You are a groundedness auditor for a read-only Horizon Bank FAQ assistant.\n        Evaluate EACH supplied task independently for whether its supplied\n        parents are response-ready: they must contain enough materially\n        relevant, grounded information for the assistant to give the customer\n        a useful FAQ response.\n\n        Original User Message (advisory context only; never use it as an\n        individual task's completeness target): what about that?\n        Trusted Conversation Context: Last Session Recall (advisory only; not current state):\nNone\n\nCurrent-Session Rolling Context (advisory only):\nNone\n\nCurrent Session Trusted History (latest 10 turns):\nAI: Welcome back, Benson! How can I help with your banking today? Also, you still have 6 pending requests (Change Address and Resubmit KYC Document) — you can check them anytime from the requests icon in the top right.\nUser: what's the rate\nAI: Could you please clarify what you mean by \"what's the rate\"? Are you asking about a deposit account, a personal loan, or a credit card? 📊\nUser: I am asking about interest rates for a deposit account.\nAI: The interest rate you receive on a Horizon Bank savings account depends on the savings plan attached to your account. If you have not selected a plan, Horizon Bank automatically places you in the Signature plan. 📊\n\nUnder the Signature plan, you may earn a combined interest of up to 1% per annum on the first S$1,200,000 of your savings balance. Here is how it is broken down:\n\n• **Base rate:** 0.05% per year applied without any conditions.\n• **Spend bonus:** 0.2% per year for Horizon Union members or 0.1% per year for non-members, provided you complete at least five qualifying card transactions each month.\n• **Balance bonus:** 0.3% per year when your average daily balance for the month reaches S$100,000.\n• **Salary bonus:** 0.45% per year if a minimum salary credit of S$1,500 is posted in a single GIRO transaction with purpose code SALA during the month.\n\nAny amount above S$1,200,000 accrues only the base rate of 0.05% per annum, and interest is credited on the last day of each month.\nUser: what's the fee\nAI: Horizon Bank does not charge any fees when you send or receive Singapore-dollar transfers into a Horizon Savings Account, and there is no fee applied if you decide to close your account 💳. Please note that interest earned during the month of closure will not be credited.\nUser: yes\nAI: Glad I could help clear that up for you today! 😊\nUser: what about that?\n        Task Inputs: [{\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"task\": {\"task_id\": \"task_1\", \"procedural\": \"Initiate account closure through the mobile app or by visiting a branch for assistance.\", \"policy\": \"No fees are applied for Singapore-dollar transfers or for closing a savings account.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit product designed for holding funds and facilitating basic money transfers.\", \"target_commercial_product\": \"Deposit_Account\", \"target_intent\": [\"Fees And Charges\", \"Payments And Transfers\", \"Account Management\"], \"customer_component\": \"Clarification on the previously discussed fee structure for Horizon Savings Account transfers and account closure.\", \"direct_query\": \"Clarification on the previously discussed fee structure for Horizon Savings Account transfers and account closure.\", \"subquery_id\": \"subquery_1\", \"customer_original_wording\": \"what about that?\", \"angle_groups\": [{\"group_id\": \"base\", \"procedural\": \"Initiate account closure through the mobile app or by visiting a branch for assistance.\", \"policy\": \"No fees are applied for Singapore-dollar transfers or for closing a savings account.\", \"conceptual\": \"A savings account is a deposit product designed for holding funds and facilitating basic money transfers.\"}]}, \"retained_partial_parent_ids\": [], \"prior_sufficiency_audit_history\": [], \"parents\": [{\"parent_id\": \"faq_df2c5fa7\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank apply any fees when I transfer money to or from my Horizon Savings Account?\\n\\nAnswer: - No, Horizon Bank does not charge any fee for sending or receiving Singapore‑dollar transfers into a Horizon Savings Account.\"}, {\"parent_id\": \"faq_a1fd1b2a\", \"content\": \"Question: Does Horizon Bank charge any fee for closing an account?\\n\\nAnswer: - No fee is applied when you close your Horizon Bank account. Interest earned during the month of closure will not be credited.\"}]}]\n\n        Rules:\n        - Each Task Input contains `task.customer_component`: the intent\n          formulator's resolved sub-query for that task. Evaluate a task ONLY\n          against its own `customer_component` and that task's candidate\n          parents. It also contains `task.customer_original_wording`: the\n          customer's own faithful wording for this task, which may be\n          plainer or vaguer than `customer_component` (which can be\n          elaborated with retrieval-oriented wording the customer never\n          actually said). Use `customer_original_wording`, never\n          `customer_component`, as the source when you set `unresolved_term`\n          below -- a clarifying question must quote something the customer\n          will recognize as their own.\n        - Each Task Input may include `prior_sufficiency_audit_history` from\n          earlier attempts for the same task in this turn. Read it before\n          judging the current candidates and remain consistent with its prior\n          sufficiency judgments. This history is internal audit context only;\n          it is not customer-facing evidence and does not authorize any new\n          factual claim.\n        - Classify each task as SUFFICIENT, PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT, or\n          INSUFFICIENT. Judge whether the supplied parents provide useful,\n          materially relevant information for the task—not whether they repeat\n          the customer's wording or explicitly resolve every possible\n          interpretation of the customer's question.\n        - PARTIAL-EVIDENCE DECISION ORDER: First identify whether any supplied\n          parent contains a factual proposition directly relevant to a\n          meaningful aspect of the customer's resolved request. If one does,\n          do not return INSUFFICIENT merely because the parent cannot determine\n          the customer's requested outcome, permission, eligibility,\n          exception, legality, preferred action, or other broader conclusion.\n          Retain that parent as PARTIALLY_SUFFICIENT when its supported fact\n          can be truthfully presented as useful, bounded Horizon guidance\n          while another material aspect remains unresolved. Continue retrieval\n          for the unresolved aspect.\n        - Return INSUFFICIENT only when no supplied parent contains any\n          factual proposition that can be truthfully and materially presented\n          in relation to the resolved request. A parent is not material merely\n          because it concerns the same product: its supported fact must\n          directly concern the same topic, condition, process, boundary, or\n          factual premise in the customer's request.\n        - The reverse matters just as much: a parent whose own subject is a\n          distinctly-named, different product or service is not material\n          merely because it is credit/loan-adjacent, belongs to the same\n          broader family, or is reached through the same in-app menu path as\n          the customer's named product. For example, a balance transfer\n          draws on loan credit and is filed under the app's \"Loan\" section\n          alongside a personal loan